---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const embed = `python scripts/embedding/embed_dataset.py \\
  --model_name Orthrus \\
  --model_version orthrus-large-6-track \\
  --dataset_name go-mf \\
  --batch_size 8`;

const chunks = `for chunk in {0..7}; do
  python scripts/embedding/embed_dataset.py \\
    --model_name Orthrus \\
    --model_version orthrus-large-6-track \\
    --dataset_name go-mf \\
    --d_chunk_ind "$chunk" \\
    --d_num_chunks 8
done`;

const probe = `python scripts/linear_probe/by_modelname.py \\
  --model_name Orthrus \\
  --model_version orthrus-large-6-track \\
  --dataset_name go-mf \\
  --task multilabel \\
  --target target \\
  --split_type homology`;

const embeddingVep = `python scripts/linear_probe/by_modelname.py \\
  --model_name Orthrus \\
  --model_version orthrus-large-4-track \\
  --dataset_name vep-traitgym-mendelian \\
  --task embedding_vep \\
  --target target`;

const embedVepDataset = `python scripts/embedding/embed_dataset.py \\
  --model_name Orthrus \\
  --model_version orthrus-large-4-track \\
  --dataset_name vep-traitgym-mendelian \\
  --batch_size 8`;

const likelihoodVep = `python scripts/linear_probe/by_modelname.py \\
  --model_name Evo2 \\
  --model_version Evo2-7B-8K \\
  --dataset_name vep-traitgym-mendelian \\
  --task likelihood_vep \\
  --target target \\
  --score_method causal_likelihood \\
  --normalization sum \\
  --attn_implementation flash_attention_2`;

const fineTune = `python scripts/finetune/run_finetune.py \\
  --model_name Orthrus \\
  --model_version orthrus-large-4-track \\
  --dataset_name mrl-sugimoto \\
  --learning_rates '[1e-5, 1e-4]' \\
  --lora_ranks '[4, 8]' \\
  --lora_alphas '[16]' \\
  --epochs 15 \\
  --batch_size 32 \\
  --seeds '[0, 1, 2]' \\
  --lr_schedule cosine \\
  --eval_test`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Run a benchmark"
  description="Persist embeddings, run probes across seeds, score variant effects, and launch optional fine-tuning."
  section="Run"
>
  <p>
    Use the in-memory quickstart for small experiments. Use repository scripts
    for full datasets, cluster jobs, and resumable output.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Generate embeddings</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={embed} language="shell" />
  <p>
    Embeddings are written below the configured dataset path. The embedder keeps
    dataframe order and passes coding-sequence and splice tracks when both the
    dataset and model use them.
  </p>

  <h3>Split a large embedding job into chunks</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={chunks} language="shell" />
  <p>
    Run every zero-based chunk index. The embedder does not create the merged
    embedding until all eight chunk files are present.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Run the probe</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={probe} language="shell" />
  <p>
    The script runs the standard seeded evaluation and writes metrics to the
    dataset's <code>results.db</code>. Use the exact task names
    <code>regression_ols</code> and <code>regression_ridge</code> when querying
    current persisted regression results.
  </p>

  <h2>Variant-effect prediction</h2>
  <h3>Embedding distance</h3>
  <p>Generate the matching dataset and model embeddings first.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={embedVepDataset} language="shell" />
  <CodeBlock code={embeddingVep} language="shell" />
  <p>
    The default embedding score is the L2 distance between pooled alternate and
    reference embeddings.
  </p>

  <h3>Likelihood scoring</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={likelihoodVep} language="shell" />
  <p>
    Available score methods are <code>causal_likelihood</code>,
    <code>pseudo_likelihood</code>, and <code>masked_marginal</code>. Masked
    marginal scoring excludes indels.
  </p>
  <Callout tone="important" label="Method detail">
    <p>
      Attention backend, dtype, pooling, normalization, and score direction are
      part of a variant-effect method. Generate reference and alternate scores
      with identical settings.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Optional fine-tuning</h2>
  <p>
    Install both optional groups first:
    <code>python -m pip install -e '.[base_models,fine_tune]'</code>.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={fineTune} language="shell" />
  <p>
    The script creates a task head, applies LoRA, selects the best validation
    state, optionally evaluates the test split, and writes a JSON result
    containing selected hyperparameters and metrics. The values passed
    through <code>--seeds</code> control data
    splitting and result identity. They do not currently seed every source of
    training randomness, so fine-tuning remains nondeterministic.
  </p>
  <Callout tone="important" label="Fine-tuning result identity">
    <p>
      The persisted filename does not include every training option. Use
      separate output directories for runs that differ only in epochs, batch
      size, accumulation, schedule, warmup, patience, attention backend, or
      test-evaluation settings.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</DocsLayout>
